Package: gPIPE
Title: Generalized PIPE Design with Epsilon-Tapering for Dose-Finding Studies
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Xiaoran", "Lai", , "research@xlai.org", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7364-3993"))
Description: Implements the Product of Independent beta Probabilities
    Escalation (PIPE) design for drug-combination dose-finding trials, for any
    number of drugs. It covers the original PIPE design for the maximum
    tolerated dose contour of Mander and Sweeting (2015) <doi:10.1002/sim.6434>
    and PIPE with epsilon-tapering for the minimum effective dose of Cheung,
    Chandereng and Diaz (2022) <doi:10.1214/21-aoas1603>. Estimates use exact
    solvers (enumeration of monotone dose sets, or a minimum cut), and whole
    trials can be simulated to give operating characteristics.
